        "original_id": "4475afae-4636-5dd7-8c11-7232c16c419b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Charles Orme, Michael Powell, Emeric Pressburger, Jacques Offenbach\n- Companies: The Archers\n- Products: The Red Shoes, The Small Back Room, Gone to Earth, The Elusive Pimpernel, The Tales of Hoffmann, Oh... Rosalinda!!\n- Roles: production assistant, production manager, assistant director\n- Topics: British Technicolor film adaptation, opera adaptation\n\nFacts:\n- In 1948, Charles Orme worked as a production assistant, production manager, and assistant director on the classic production The Red Shoes.\n- In 1949, Charles Orme worked as a production assistant, production manager, and assistant director on The Small Back Room.\n- In 1950, Charles Orme worked as a production assistant, production manager, and assistant director on Gone to Earth and The Elusive Pimpernel.\n- In 1951, Charles Orme worked as a production assistant, production manager, and assistant director on The Tales of Hoffmann.\n- In 1951, The Tales of Hoffmann was released as a British Technicolor film adaptation of Jacques Offenbach's opera The Tales of Hoffmann.\n- In 1951, Michael Powell and Emeric Pressburger wrote, produced, and directed The Tales of Hoffmann under their production company, The Archers.\n- Charles Orme also worked as a production assistant, production manager, and assistant director on Oh... Rosalinda!!.",
